## Machine-Readable Interfaces


- [OpenAPI specification](https://www.pixelcut.ai/openapi.json): The full OpenAPI 3.1 description of the Pixelcut REST API — every endpoint, typed request and response schema, error codes, and both authentication schemes (`X-API-Key` for server-to-server calls, OAuth 2.0 with the `pixa:read` and `pixa:write` scopes for integrations acting on a user's behalf). Also served as YAML at https://www.pixelcut.ai/openapi.yaml. Use this to generate a client or a function-calling tool definition.
- [MCP server](https://mcp.pixelcut.ai/mcp): Pixelcut's Model Context Protocol server, over Streamable HTTP, exposing the editing tools natively to MCP clients. Authorizes with OAuth 2.0; the server card is at https://www.pixelcut.ai/.well-known/mcp.json and protected-resource metadata (RFC 9728) at https://mcp.pixelcut.ai/.well-known/oauth-protected-resource.
- [Get an API key](https://www.pixelcut.ai/developer-settings): Self-serve API key generation — create a free account and generate a key here, with no sales contact and no waiting list. New accounts start with free credits, so an integration can be tested end to end before any payment.
- [API errors](https://www.pixelcut.ai/docs/api-reference): Every API error is JSON with a human-readable `error` and a stable machine-readable `error_code` (for example `file_size_too_large`, `insufficient_credits`, `invalid_auth_token`), enumerated per endpoint in the OpenAPI specification.


